🔒 2. final Keyword

The `final` keyword is used to restrict modifications.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 final Variable

```java id="f1"
final int MAX = 100;
```

✔ Value cannot be changed.

---

🔹 final Method

```java id="f2"
final void display() {
    System.out.println("Final Method");
}
```

✔ Cannot be overridden.

---

🔹 final Class

```java id="f3"
final class Vehicle {
}
```

✔ Cannot be inherited.

---

📌 Summary

| Usage          | Purpose             |
| -------------- | ------------------- |
| final variable | Constant value      |
| final method   | Prevent overriding  |
| final class    | Prevent inheritance |

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧹 3. finally Block

The `finally` block executes whether an exception occurs or not.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="fi1"
try {
}
catch(Exception e) {
}
finally {
}
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="fi2"
try {
    int result = 10 / 0;
}
catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("Exception Handled");
}
finally {
    System.out.println("Finally Executed");
}
```

---

📌 Output

```text id="fi3"
Exception Handled
Finally Executed
```

---

🎯 Uses of finally

✔ Closing files
✔ Closing database connections
✔ Resource cleanup

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

♻️ 4. finalize() Method

The `finalize()` method is called by the Garbage Collector before destroying an object.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="fz1"
protected void finalize() {
    System.out.println("Finalize Called");
}
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="fz2"
class Demo {

    protected void finalize() {
        System.out.println("Object Removed");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Demo obj = new Demo();

        obj = null;

        System.gc();
    }
}
```

---

⚠️ Important Note

`finalize()` has been deprecated in modern Java versions.

👉 It should not be used for resource cleanup.

---

✅ Modern Alternative

Use:

```java id="fz3"
try-with-resources
```

for automatic resource management.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 final vs finally vs finalize()

| Feature                | final                   | finally            | finalize()         |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------ |
| Type                   | Keyword                 | Block              | Method             |
| Purpose                | Restriction             | Cleanup execution  | GC callback        |
| Used With              | Variable, Method, Class | Exception Handling | Garbage Collection |
| Executes Automatically | ❌ No                    | ✔ Yes              | ✔ By GC            |
| Recommended Today      | ✔ Yes                   | ✔ Yes              | ❌ Deprecated       |

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Confusing `final` with `finally`
❌ Using `finalize()` for cleanup
❌ Forgetting `finally` for resource management

---

🧠 Real Insight

👉 In modern Java:

* `final` is widely used
* `finally` is commonly used
* `finalize()` is rarely used and deprecated

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ `try-catch` handles exceptions
✔ `final` restricts modifications
✔ `finally` always executes after try/catch
✔ `finalize()` is called before object destruction
✔ `finalize()` is deprecated in modern Java

